.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd September 6, 2026
.Dt SYS-INIT-TEST-NATIVE-IO-STOP 1
.Os sys-init experimental
.Sh NAME
.Nm sys-init-test-native-io-stop
.Nd consume experimental sys-init artifacts in an isolated Aether test workspace
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm python3
.Ar tests/native-io-stop.py
.br
.Fl Fl aether Ar directory
.br
.Fl Fl sdk Ar directory
.br
.Fl Fl receipt-pin Ar digest
.br
.Fl Fl work Ar directory
.br
.Op Fl Fl peer | Fl Fl authority
.br
.Op Fl Fl readiness | Fl Fl retained
.Nm python3
.Ar tests/native-io-stop.py
.Fl Fl help
.Nm python3
.Ar tests/native-io-stop.py
.Fl Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This source-checkout developer command performs actual kernel builds and
native
QEMU smoke tests.
It is not an installed operator command, a host-only model
check or permission to test arbitrary images.
Use trusted, independently reviewed
inputs and tools matching the selected retained experiment.
The command copies inputs to a new workspace and builds there rather than in
the original kernel tree.
Existing workspace paths are rejected.
No root privileges, host service installation or physical target access is
needed.
.Pp
Use Python 3.10 or newer, Rust 1.98.0 with x86_64-unknown-none and a
producer-compatible Zig/QEMU toolchain with boot dependencies already
available.
The wrapper does not select a kernel revision for you or authenticate
provenance
merely by copying and hashing a mutable directory.
Provision tools separately.
The SDK receipt digest, selected profile, bounded AENATC01 envelope and
startup
ELF/payload digests are validated before the workspace is created.
The runner
copies the kernel, SDK envelope/receipt and sys-init builder inputs, including
the bounded_tools.py import.
Captured files are hashed before commands and
rechecked after successful completion.
.Pp
Default cases cover stop, wrong-detail, skip-zero and original-I/O
compatibility.
Retained mode covers retained-stop, retained-fault, wrong-kind and skip-zero.
Readiness mode covers five exit/fault/stop orderings plus invent-ready and
skip-zero.
Authority mode covers authority, allow-notify and skip-zero.
Peer
mode covers peer, peer-reverse, wrong-peer and skip-zero.
The runner uses SMP=false and native-memory=false, exact smoke exits/markers,
selected semantic rejection contexts and real fault markers where required.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl Fl aether Ar directory
Trusted kernel source snapshot with matching boot dependencies.
.It Fl Fl sdk Ar directory
Reviewed SDK containing evidence.json and native-c.bin.
.It Fl Fl receipt-pin Ar digest
Externally retained SHA-256 of the SDK evidence.json.
.It Fl Fl work Ar directory
New workspace; must not already exist.
.It Fl Fl retained
Require an io-retained worker receipt and select retained-output cases.
.It Fl Fl readiness
Require io-readiness and select readiness/terminal ordering cases.
.It Fl Fl authority
Require io-authority and select caller-local authority cases.
.It Fl Fl peer
Require io-peer and select peer-readiness cases.
.It Fl Fl help
Print usage and exit without creating a workspace or launching tools.
.It Fl Fl version
Print the harness-command version and exit, not a published release version.
.El
.Pp
All four profile flags are mutually exclusive, including across the two groups
shown for wrapping in the synopsis.
With no profile flag, require probe_variant io.
Relative input/work paths are resolved from the caller's working directory.
Do not place the new workspace inside any input tree: the harness copies those
trees and does not uniformly enforce that separation.
Reserve a private path
outside producer/SDK/dependency directories and preserve failed workspaces.
.Sh OUTPUT AND FILES
Per-case [OK] progress goes to standard error; success prints JSON with result
and report path on standard output. results.json starts with result running
and
contains commands, case oracles and artifact hashes.
Its schema distinguishes
stop, retained, readiness, authority and peer profiles. sources.json, copied
SDK inputs, sys-init/, Aether/, clients/ and serial/tool logs remain
available.
A caught command timeout is recorded, then the outer exception path records
final failure; an interruption caught in the command wait retains interrupted.
Setup failure or abrupt termination can leave no final report.
.Pp
A running, missing, incomplete or failed report is not passing evidence.
Do not erase unsuccessful attempts or substitute a previous passing report for
current inputs.
A passing guest run applies only to its selected frozen profile.
.Sh LIMITS AND ENVIRONMENT
The host environment selects tools through PATH; Python and producer smoke
scripts can inherit other host settings.
There is no downloader or hosted CI
setup in this command.
A copy/hash record alone is not a live sandbox guarantee.
Tool commands have 120-second wait deadlines and owned sessions.
Timeout/interruption cleanup kills the owned trusted, non-detaching process
group.
Logs stream to files without a separate size cap.
Copying and hashing are outside
these per-command deadlines; there is no overall suite deadline.
Guest smoke
watchdogs are separate producer-owned behavior, not a substitute for host
bounds.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
All selected cases completed successfully, or a supported help/version query.
.It 1
An ordinary Python exception or explicit semantic/build rejection.
Other interpreter/signal termination statuses are possible.
.It 64
Invalid usage or incompatible required option combinations.
.It 130
Interruption caught while waiting for a child command.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
From the repository root, inspect usage without starting a guest:
.Bd -literal -offset left
python3 tests/native-io-stop.py --help
.Ed
.Pp
A full invocation below starts real builds/QEMU.
First set the quoted shell
variables from an independently reviewed handoff; they are placeholders, not
harness environment settings.
WORK must name a new private directory outside
all input trees.
No root privileges are required.
.Bd -literal -offset left
python3 tests/native-io-stop.py \e
  --aether "$AETHER" --sdk "$SDK" \e
  --receipt-pin "$RECEIPT_PIN" --work "$WORK"
.Ed
.Pp
Expect all selected cases, exit zero and the documented outputs on success.
Retain the entire workspace on failure; do not rerun into an existing
workspace.
.Sh SEE ALSO
Repository guides: docs/NATIVE-COVERAGE.md, docs/LIFECYCLE-V1.md,
docs/NATIVE-SUPERVISION.md, docs/NATIVE-IO.md, docs/NATIVE-ADAPTER.md
and docs/DOCUMENTATION-INVENTORY.md.
Exact retained decisions define compatible
producer inputs and test oracles; manuals do not replace those contracts.
.Sh CAVEATS
Independent technical/reader review and installed-target manual lookup remain
pending.
The native init profiles are experiments, not production POSIX init.
